<id/16/1698/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Annotto"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_natural_dyestuffs/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a dye-stuff prepared from the red pulp of the seeds of the *Bixa orellana*, which enters into commerce under two forms, flag and roll. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 24]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_natural_dyestuffs): Named dye or pigment (annotto, orchella, weld, rock moss = orchil lichen per Mortimer 1823 s.v. ROCK MOSS 'See ORCHILLA', vermilion, zaffre, verdigris, lampblack) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 6 rows, 1800–1834. Series: KEW_CUST 5 ×4; KEW_CUST 4 ×2. Units: CWTS (Hundredweights) ×4; Hundredweights.Quarters.Pounds ×2. Top routes: Canada → England ×2; World → United Kingdom ×1; Portugal and Madeira → United Kingdom ×1; Ireland → United Kingdom ×1."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "1698" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Annotto"@en ;
